So let's say you want to add searchForFacetValues to your refinement list: 

```js
render()
{
  const facetHits = this.props.facetHits.map(facet = > {
    return 
    <label>
      <input type="checkbox"
             checked={facet.isRefined}
             onChange={() => {
               this.props.refine(facet.value)
             }}/>
      {facet.value}
    </label>
  }
)
  return (
    <div>
      <input onChange={e => {
        this.props.searchForFacetValues(e.target.value)
      }}
             type="search"/>
      {facetHits}
      {/* markup of the refinement list*/}
    </div>);
}
```

This is of course not a complete working example, it's just to give you an idea of the usage of the `searchforFacetValues` and how to retrieve the `facetsHits`.

IMO we should just modify our current connector and widget. As for the widget, displaying the input should be configurable through a prop.
